(a) the time interval between the eventsA and B in the reference frame where the two events occurred at the same point; 
(b) the distance between the points at which the events A and C occurred in the reference frame where these two events are simultaneous.

statement:
Two particles move toward each other with velocities $v_1 = 0.50 c$ and $v_2 = 0.75 c$ relative to the laboratory frame. Find:
